Integrity convention (from CZ-IR 1.0, sections 10.4 and 10.5):
Any version, amendment, or translation of the Core must preserve its version
identifier, publication date, change history, contributors, reasons for change,
evidence relied upon, and unresolved objections; and must expose how it maps to
the Core. No revision may silently replace the origin. CZ-CORE 1.0 remains
permanently accessible in its original form.
